WEBVTT

00:00:03.786 --> 00:00:06.266
-Better than me?
-(CLEARS THROAT)

00:00:07.146 --> 00:00:08.666
I mean, she's good.

00:00:08.826 --> 00:00:10.866
(STAMMERING)
Really, a credit to her...

00:00:11.026 --> 00:00:13.626
You know. (CHUCKLES NERVOUSLY)
You know.

00:00:13.826 --> 00:00:14.866
With great respect...

00:00:15.026 --> 00:00:16.266
let's not test the whole

00:00:16.346 --> 00:00:17.946
"insurance-will-pay-
for-everything" idea...

00:00:18.106 --> 00:00:20.346
-on the first go 'round, okay?
-(FROZONE CHUCKLES)

00:00:20.426 --> 00:00:23.826
Wait a minute.
You're saying what? I'm messy?

00:00:23.986 --> 00:00:25.866
Well, Evelyn did
a cost-benefit analysis...

00:00:26.026 --> 00:00:28.266
comparing all your last
five years of crime fighting

00:00:28.346 --> 00:00:29.946
before going underground.

00:00:30.106 --> 00:00:31.946
And Elastigirl's numbers
are self-explanatory.

00:00:32.106 --> 00:00:34.026
Well, it's not
a fair comparison!

00:00:34.186 --> 00:00:36.746
Heavyweight problems
need heavyweight solutions.

00:00:36.906 --> 00:00:38.466
Of course! We're gonna solve

00:00:38.546 --> 00:00:40.506
all kinds
of problems together.

00:00:40.666 --> 00:00:45.026
After the perfect launch
with Elastigirl!

00:00:45.866 --> 00:00:47.626
So, what do you say?

00:00:48.306 --> 00:00:50.626
What do I say? (CHUCKLES)

00:00:51.586 --> 00:00:53.706
I don't know.

00:00:53.906 --> 00:00:55.586
What do you mean,
you don't know?

00:00:55.746 --> 00:00:57.906
A few hours ago,
you were saying it was over...

00:00:58.066 --> 00:01:00.186
and being a superhero
was a fantasy.

00:01:00.346 --> 00:01:02.186
Now, you get the offer
of a lifetime

00:01:02.266 --> 00:01:03.546
and you don't know?

00:01:03.746 --> 00:01:06.866
It's not that simple, Bob.
I wanna protect the kids!

00:01:07.026 --> 00:01:08.426
So do I.

00:01:08.626 --> 00:01:10.226
From jail, Bob!

00:01:10.386 --> 00:01:11.546
-(SPITS)
-BOB: And how do you do that?

00:01:11.706 --> 00:01:13.906
By turning down a chance
to change the law

00:01:13.986 --> 00:01:15.346
that forces them to hide
what they are?

00:01:15.546 --> 00:01:17.906
They haven't decided what
they are. They're still kids.

00:01:18.066 --> 00:01:20.426
Kids with powers,
which makes them Supers...

00:01:20.586 --> 00:01:22.866
whether they decide
to use those powers or not.

00:01:23.026 --> 00:01:24.146
This will benefit them.

00:01:24.346 --> 00:01:26.146
It's not a good time
to be away.

00:01:26.306 --> 00:01:27.746
Dash is having trouble
with homework...

00:01:27.906 --> 00:01:29.666
Vi is worried
about her first date

00:01:29.746 --> 00:01:31.026
with that boy she likes,
Tony...

00:01:31.186 --> 00:01:32.186
and Jack-Jack...

00:01:32.346 --> 00:01:34.146
Jack-Jack?
What's wrong with him?

00:01:35.106 --> 00:01:36.306
Okay, nothing's wrong
with Jack-Jack.

00:01:36.466 --> 00:01:39.026
But even a normal baby
needs a lot of attention.

00:01:39.186 --> 00:01:40.786
I'm just not sure I can leave.

00:01:40.946 --> 00:01:42.186
Of course you can leave.

00:01:42.346 --> 00:01:44.346
You've got to. So that I...

00:01:44.506 --> 00:01:46.306
we can be Supers again,

00:01:46.386 --> 00:01:48.066
so our kids can have
that choice.

00:01:48.346 --> 00:01:50.026
(SCOFFS)
So you can have that choice.

00:01:50.186 --> 00:01:51.346
All right, yes!

00:01:51.546 --> 00:01:53.706
So I can have that choice.

00:01:54.106 --> 00:01:56.466
And I would do a great job!

00:01:56.626 --> 00:02:00.826
Regardless of what Deavor's
pie charts say or whatever...

00:02:00.986 --> 00:02:03.026
But they want you.

00:02:03.186 --> 00:02:05.746
(STRAINED)
And you'll do a great...

00:02:06.666 --> 00:02:07.906
job...

00:02:08.506 --> 00:02:09.706
too.

00:02:11.426 --> 00:02:13.906
(INHALES SHARPLY) Well, that
was excruciating to watch.

00:02:14.466 --> 00:02:16.386
-(CHUCKLES)
-I can't lie to you.

00:02:16.546 --> 00:02:19.546
It's nice to be wanted.
Flattering, you know, but...

00:02:19.706 --> 00:02:20.706
But what's the choice?

00:02:20.786 --> 00:02:22.026
One, do this right,

00:02:22.106 --> 00:02:23.306
get well paid,
we're out of the motel...

00:02:23.466 --> 00:02:25.266
and things get better
for all Supers,

00:02:25.346 --> 00:02:26.506
including our kids.

00:02:26.706 --> 00:02:28.226
Or two...

00:02:28.386 --> 00:02:30.826
I find a job in two weeks
or we're homeless.

00:02:31.666 --> 00:02:33.226
You know it's crazy, right?

00:02:33.386 --> 00:02:35.506
To help my family,
I gotta leave it.

00:02:35.666 --> 00:02:36.746
To fix the law,
I gotta break it.

00:02:36.826 --> 00:02:37.826
You'll be great.

00:02:37.906 --> 00:02:38.906
I know I will.

00:02:38.986 --> 00:02:40.146
But what about you?
We have kids.

00:02:40.306 --> 00:02:41.866
I'll watch the kids,
no problem.

00:02:42.026 --> 00:02:43.546
-Easy.
-Easy, huh?

00:02:43.706 --> 00:02:45.266
You're adorable.

00:02:45.426 --> 00:02:46.426
Well, if there is a problem,

00:02:46.506 --> 00:02:47.746
I'll drop this thing
and come right back.

00:02:47.906 --> 00:02:49.106
You won't need to.

00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:51.266
I got it,
you go do this thing.

00:02:51.946 --> 00:02:53.986
Do it so...

00:02:54.146 --> 00:02:56.266
I can do it better. (GRUNTS)

00:02:56.626 --> 00:02:58.706
-(PHONE RINGS)
-Deavor here.

00:02:58.866 --> 00:03:00.186
This is Elastigirl.

00:03:00.346 --> 00:03:01.386
I'm in.

00:03:04.826 --> 00:03:07.386
Mr. Deavor, it's wonderful...

00:03:07.546 --> 00:03:09.026
but it's too generous.

00:03:09.186 --> 00:03:10.426
Nonsense!
That's the least we can do.

00:03:10.626 --> 00:03:12.066
We're partners now!

00:03:12.146 --> 00:03:13.906
Can't have my partners
living in a motel.

00:03:14.066 --> 00:03:16.506
(STAMMERS) But whose house?
Is it a house?

00:03:16.666 --> 00:03:18.186
WINSTON: It's my house.
I have several.

00:03:18.266 --> 00:03:20.666
I'm not using that one.
Stay as long as you need.

00:03:20.826 --> 00:03:22.306
I don't know what to say.

00:03:22.466 --> 00:03:24.466
How about "thanks"?

00:03:25.506 --> 00:03:27.466
This is our new house?

00:03:27.626 --> 00:03:30.746
(CHUCKLES) Okay, easy, tiger.
It's being loaned to us.

00:03:30.826 --> 00:03:32.786
(GROANS) This is homey.

00:03:32.946 --> 00:03:34.066
BOB: Look at this place.

00:03:34.146 --> 00:03:36.826
Deavor bought it from
an eccentric billionaire...

00:03:37.026 --> 00:03:38.546
who liked to come and go
without being seen...

00:03:38.706 --> 00:03:41.106
so the house
has multiple hidden exits.

00:03:41.266 --> 00:03:42.786
Good thing we won't stand out.

00:03:42.986 --> 00:03:45.746
Wouldn't want to attract
any unnecessary attention.

00:03:45.946 --> 00:03:47.866
DASH: It's got a big yard!

00:03:48.026 --> 00:03:49.946
Isn't this a bit much?

00:03:50.106 --> 00:03:51.906
Near a forest!

00:03:52.066 --> 00:03:53.706
Would you rather be
at the motel?

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:56.146
-DASH: And a pool!
-(SPLASH)

00:03:56.306 --> 00:03:58.466
What exactly is Mom's new job?

00:03:58.626 --> 00:04:00.866
The important thing is
we're out of the motel.

00:04:01.026 --> 00:04:03.346
I like Mom's new job!

00:04:04.466 --> 00:04:06.386
(GASPS) Oh, ho, ho!

00:04:09.626 --> 00:04:12.066
-BOB: Whoa.
-(BOTH CHUCKLE)

00:04:12.266 --> 00:04:13.426
Whoa.

00:04:15.546 --> 00:04:17.626
Well, check out
the water features.

00:04:17.706 --> 00:04:19.066
(HELEN CHUCKLES)

00:04:19.986 --> 00:04:21.266
-(CHUCKLES) Oh!
-Wow.

00:04:23.346 --> 00:04:24.906
Wicked cool!

00:04:25.426 --> 00:04:26.506
(BOB CHUCKLES)

00:04:30.986 --> 00:04:32.386
-Hey! Dash! Stop it!
-(GROANS)

00:04:32.546 --> 00:04:34.306
-Not the couch! Stop it!
-No! Dash!

00:04:34.386 --> 00:04:35.626
-(GRUNTING)
-BOB: Stop!

00:04:35.706 --> 00:04:36.906
-Don't touch the buttons!
-DASH: The couch!

00:04:37.066 --> 00:04:38.066
HELEN: Dash!
BOB: No!

00:04:38.146 --> 00:04:40.026
-(WHIMPERS)
-BOB: No, no!

00:04:40.186 --> 00:04:41.866
HELEN: Oh, no.
Oh, boy.

00:04:42.306 --> 00:04:43.986
ELASTIGIRL: This isn't me.
(STAMMERING)

00:04:44.066 --> 00:04:45.666
(JACK-JACK COOING)

00:04:46.506 --> 00:04:49.626
I'm not all dark and angsty.

00:04:49.786 --> 00:04:50.866
I'm Elastigirl.

00:04:51.026 --> 00:04:52.826
I'm, you know, flexible.

00:04:52.986 --> 00:04:54.226
E designed this?

00:04:54.386 --> 00:04:57.266
No, some guy named
Alexander Galbaki.

00:04:57.346 --> 00:04:59.466
(CHUCKLING)
Glad it's you and not me,

00:04:59.546 --> 00:05:01.986
'cause you're gonna
hear from her.

00:05:02.146 --> 00:05:03.346
This note came with it.

00:05:03.506 --> 00:05:04.506
What?

00:05:06.906 --> 00:05:08.106
(DOOR BEEPS)

00:05:08.786 --> 00:05:10.066
(GASPS)

00:05:11.426 --> 00:05:13.466
A new Elasticycle.

00:05:13.666 --> 00:05:16.146
Elasticycle?
I didn't know you had a bike.

00:05:16.306 --> 00:05:17.506
Hey, I had a mohawk.

00:05:17.626 --> 00:05:18.986
There's a lot about me
you don't know.

00:05:19.146 --> 00:05:21.026
Yeah, but...
A mohawk?

00:05:21.186 --> 00:05:23.426
Ah, you didn't miss anything.

00:05:23.506 --> 00:05:24.946
(POWERING UP)

00:05:25.866 --> 00:05:28.226
Oh, yeah!
This one's electric.

00:05:28.426 --> 00:05:31.346
-What's that mean?
-Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa.

00:05:33.026 --> 00:05:34.306
(GROANS)

00:05:34.386 --> 00:05:37.026
Means it's torque-y.
I'll get the hang of it.

00:05:37.146 --> 00:05:38.186
You will be great.

00:05:38.266 --> 00:05:40.146
I will be great.
And you will, too.

00:05:40.306 --> 00:05:41.786
We will both be great.

00:05:41.986 --> 00:05:43.106
Bye, sweetie.

